</style></head><body><main><div class="eyebrow">Gojo · reusable rules and revisable participation</div><h1>The same question, different worlds; the same template, different assumptions</h1><p class="intro">A connected rule pack can inspect ornament, glyph and route constructions without receiving their domain labels. A separate generation experiment asks how a provisional shared parameter survives partial evidence, conflict and revision.</p><div class="links"><a href="overview.html">All constructions</a><a href="../ornament-defaults/gallery.html">Requirements and defaults</a><a href="../ornament-concepts/gallery.html">Concept alternatives</a></div>
<div class="tabs" role="tablist"><button id="transfer-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="transfer">Transfer a rule pack</button><button id="generation-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="generation">Generate and revise</button></div>
<section id="transfer" role="tabpanel"><div class="controls"><label>Connected question pack<select id="pack"></select></label><label>Context and receiver services<select id="context"></select></label><label>Presentation domain<select id="domain"><option value="all">All domains</option><option value="ORNAMENT">Ornament</option><option value="GLYPH">Glyph</option><option value="NETWORK">Network</option></select></label><label>Show candidates<select id="display"><option value="all">All constructions</option><option value="eligible">Still possible</option><option value="excluded">Outside required claims</option></select></label><label class="check"><input id="groups" type="checkbox">Mechanical groups</label></div><section class="explanation"><h2 id="pack-name"></h2><p id="pack-note"></p><p id="context-note" class="hint"></p><div id="transfer-summary" class="summary"></div><details><summary>Inspect the exposed questions</summary><div id="pack-rules"></div></details><p class="muted">Domain headings organize this page. They are absent from the rule pack and do not decide admission. A required contradiction differs from a default departure; missing receiver services remain unresolved.</p></section>
<section id="inspection" class="inspection" hidden><div class="section-head"><h2 id="inspect-title"></h2><button id="close-inspection">Close details</button></div><p id="inspect-note"></p><img id="inspect-image" alt="Inspected native construction"><p id="inspect-outcome" class="hint"></p><p class="scroll-note">On narrow screens, scroll the table sideways for expectations and policy decisions.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Actual supplied question</th><th>Observed fact</th><th>Expectation</th><th>Authority</th><th>Policy read</th></tr></thead><tbody id="inspect-facts"></tbody></table></div></section><div id="transfer-cards" class="cards"></div></section>
<section id="generation" role="tabpanel" hidden><div class="controls generation-controls"><label>Executable symbolic template<select id="scenario"></select></label><label>Evidence and revision stage<select id="stage"></select></label></div><section class="explanation"><h2 id="scenario-name"></h2><p id="scenario-note"></p><div class="hint">A prior can suggest that H and V share one parameter. That proposal is not source evidence. The output checks its own realized program; it does not establish what the supplier knows.</div></section><div id="timeline" class="timeline"></div><h2 id="stage-name"></h2><p id="stage-note"></p><div class="comparisons"><figure><figcaption>Supplier drawing · inspection view</figcaption><img id="generation-source" alt="Supplier construction for comparison"><small>This full rendering is shown to the reader. The receiving engine uses only the evidence available at the selected stage.</small></figure><figure><figcaption id="generation-output-label"></figcaption><img id="generation-output" alt="Actual generated construction"><div id="generation-no-output" class="no-output" hidden></div><small id="generation-output-note"></small></figure></div><div id="generation-reads" class="read-grid"></div><div id="generation-summary" class="hint"></div><h3 style="margin-top:24px">Competing parameter hypotheses</h3><p class="scroll-note">Source compatibility, the contextual sharing prior and selection remain separate reads. Scroll the table sideways on narrow screens.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Proposal</th><th>Source evidence</th><th>Sharing relation</th><th>Contextual prior</th><th>Preference and selection</th></tr></thead><tbody id="proposals"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="findings"><h2>Findings</h2><ul id="findings"></ul><details><summary>Scope and unresolved mechanics</summary><ul id="limits"></ul></details></section><footer id="run-note"></footer></main><script src="data.js"></script><script>
(()=>{'use strict';const d=globalThis.RULE_PACK_TRANSFER,$=id=>document.getElementById(id),esc=v=>String(v??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));let selected=null;const tiers=['Required','Strong default','Preference','Unused'];const pack=()=>d.packs.find(p=>p.id===$('pack').value)||d.packs[0];const context=()=>pack().contexts.find(c=>c.id===$('context').value)||pack().contexts[0];const scenario=()=>d.generation.find(g=>g.id===$('scenario').value)||d.generation[0];const stage=()=>scenario().stages.find(s=>s.id===$('stage').value)||scenario().stages[0];const image=c=>$('groups').checked?c.groupImage:c.image;const range=(a,b)=>a===b?String(a):a+'–'+b;
function status(r){return r.answer==='No'?'Outside required claims':r.answer==='Blocked'?'Required read blocked':r.answer==='Open'?'Required read unresolved':'Contract agrees'}
function outcome(value){return({Yes:'Agrees',No:'Conflicts with expectation',Open:'Unresolved',Blocked:'Read blocked',Unused:'Carried unused',Waived:'Waived; evidence retained'})[value]||value}
function evidence(f){return f.tier===3?'Uncommitted':f.waived?'Waived '+(f.expected?'Yes':'No'):f.expected?'Yes':'No'}
function readFor(id){return d.reads.find(r=>r.pack===pack().id&&r.context===context().id&&r.case===id)}
function selectContext(){const p=pack();$('context').innerHTML=p.contexts.map(c=>'<option value="'+esc(c.id)+'">'+esc(c.name)+'</option>').join('');renderTransfer()}
function inspect(id){const c=d.cases.find(c=>c.id===id),r=readFor(id);if(!c||!r){selected=null;$('inspection').hidden=true;return}selected=id;$('inspection').hidden=false;$('inspect-title').textContent=c.id+' · '+c.name;$('inspect-note').textContent=c.note;$('inspect-image').src=image(c);$('inspect-outcome').textContent=status(r)+'. Strong defaults: '+range(r.strongLower,r.strongUpper)+' departures; preferences: '+range(r.weakLower,r.weakUpper)+'. '+(r.transportSame===true?'The independently imported pack preserved this result.':r.transportSame===false?'Independent transport did not preserve this result.':'');$('inspect-facts').innerHTML=r.facts.map((f,i)=>'<tr data-fact="'+i+'"><td>'+esc(f.label)+'</td><td class="fact">'+esc(f.answer)+'</td><td>'+esc(evidence(f))+'</td><td>'+esc(f.waived?'Waived '+tiers[f.tier]:tiers[f.tier])+'</td><td>'+esc(outcome(f.decision))+'</td></tr>').join('')}
function renderTransfer(){const p=pack(),c=context();$('pack-name').textContent=p.name;$('pack-note').textContent=p.note;$('context-note').textContent=c.note;$('pack-rules').innerHTML='<ul>'+p.rules.map(r=>'<li>'+esc(r.label)+' <small>· '+esc(r.predicateParticipants)+' native predicate participants</small></li>').join('')+'</ul>';const designs=d.cases.filter(c=>$('domain').value==='all'||c.domain===$('domain').value);const reads=designs.map(c=>readFor(c.id));$('transfer-summary').innerHTML=[[reads.filter(r=>r.eligible).length,'still possible'],[reads.filter(r=>!r.eligible).length,'outside required claims'],[reads.filter(r=>r.answer==='Open').length,'unresolved requirements']].map(([n,label])=>'<span><strong>'+n+'</strong>'+label+'</span>').join('');const shown=designs.filter(c=>{const r=readFor(c.id);return $('display').value==='all'||$('display').value==='eligible'&&r.eligible||$('display').value==='excluded'&&!r.eligible});$('transfer-cards').innerHTML=shown.length?shown.map(c=>{const r=readFor(c.id);return '<article class="card '+(!r.eligible?'excluded':r.answer==='Open'?'open':'')+'" data-case="'+esc(c.id)+'"><div class="card-head"><h3><span class="id">'+esc(c.id)+' · '+esc(c.domain.toLowerCase())+'</span>'+esc(c.name)+'</h3><span class="pill">'+esc(status(r))+'</span></div><img loading="lazy" src="'+esc(image(c))+'" alt="'+esc(c.name)+'"><div class="card-body"><p class="muted">'+esc(c.note)+'</p><p>Strong defaults: '+esc(range(r.strongLower,r.strongUpper))+' departures<br>Preferences: '+esc(range(r.weakLower,r.weakUpper))+'</p><button class="inspect" data-inspect="'+esc(c.id)+'">Inspect actual question receipts</button></div></article>'}).join(''):'<p class="empty">No constructions meet this display filter.</p>';$('transfer-cards').querySelectorAll('[data-inspect]').forEach(button=>button.onclick=()=>{inspect(button.dataset.inspect);$('inspection').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'start'})});if(selected)inspect(selected)}
function selectScenario(){const g=scenario();$('stage').innerHTML=g.stages.map(s=>'<option value="'+esc(s.id)+'">'+esc(s.name)+'</option>').join('');renderGeneration()}
function renderGeneration(){const g=scenario(),s=stage();$('scenario-name').textContent=g.name;$('scenario-note').textContent=g.note;$('stage-name').textContent=s.name;$('stage-note').textContent=s.note;$('generation-source').src=g.sourceImage;const output=s.image||s.previousImage;$('generation-output').hidden=!output;$('generation-no-output').hidden=!!output;if(output){$('generation-output').src=output;$('generation-output').classList.toggle('ghost',!s.image)}else{$('generation-output').removeAttribute('src');$('generation-no-output').textContent='No new realization is available at this stage.'}$('generation-output-label').textContent=s.image?'Actual output of the selected hypothesis':s.previousImage?'Retained earlier output · no new realization':'No output';$('generation-output-note').textContent=s.image?'This is a newly executed native template under the chosen bindings.':s.previousImage?'The faded drawing is history, not an accepted output of the current stage.':'The unresolved state is preserved rather than filled with a fabricated drawing.';$('generation-reads').innerHTML=[['Supplier H/V equality evidence',s.sourceEquality],['Selected parameter proposal',s.selected?(s.sharedAssumed?'Shared parameter':'Independent parameters'):'None selected'],['Coarse arrangement read',s.coarse],['Output / hypothesis conformance',s.outputConformance]].map(([name,value])=>'<div class="read-box">'+esc(name)+'<strong>'+esc(value)+'</strong></div>').join('');$('generation-summary').textContent='Realization: '+s.answer+'. '+s.eligible+' hypotheses remain compatible with supplied evidence; '+s.frontier+' are undominated under the selected prior. Carried participation: '+s.carried+'; withdrawn participation: '+s.withdrawn+'.';$('timeline').innerHTML=g.stages.map(t=>'<button class="stage-button" data-stage="'+esc(t.id)+'" aria-selected="'+(t.id===s.id)+'"><strong>'+esc(t.name)+'</strong>'+((t.image||t.previousImage)?'<img loading="lazy" class="'+(!t.image?'ghost':'')+'" src="'+esc(t.image||t.previousImage)+'" alt="'+esc(t.image?'Realized output':'Retained earlier output')+'">':'')+'<span>'+esc(t.image?'Native output':t.previousImage?'Earlier output retained':'No output')+'</span><span>Source equality: '+esc(t.sourceEquality)+'</span></button>').join('');$('timeline').querySelectorAll('[data-stage]').forEach(button=>button.onclick=()=>{$('stage').value=button.dataset.stage;renderGeneration()});$('proposals').innerHTML=s.proposals.map(p=>'<tr class="'+(p.selected?'proposal-selected':'')+'" data-proposal="'+esc(p.id)+'"><td>'+esc(p.name)+'</td><td>'+esc(p.sourceEligible?'Compatible':'Contradicted or blocked')+'<br><small>'+esc(p.sourceOpen)+' open; '+esc(p.sourceRefuted)+' refuted</small></td><td>'+esc(p.sharing)+'</td><td>'+esc(outcome(p.defaultDecision))+'</td><td>'+esc(p.selected?'Selected':p.frontier?'Undominated':'Not selected')+'</td></tr>').join('')||'<tr><td colspan="5">No interpretable proposal is available.</td></tr>'}
function tab(which){for(const id of ['transfer','generation']){$(id).hidden=id!==which;$(id+'-tab').setAttribute('aria-selected',id===which)}}
$('pack').innerHTML=d.packs.map(p=>'<option value="'+esc(p.id)+'">'+esc(p.name)+'</option>').join('');$('scenario').innerHTML=d.generation.map(g=>'<option value="'+esc(g.id)+'">'+esc(g.name)+'</option>').join('');$('pack').onchange=selectContext;for(const id of ['context','domain','display','groups'])$(id).onchange=renderTransfer;$('scenario').onchange=selectScenario;$('stage').onchange=renderGeneration;$('close-inspection').onclick=()=>{selected=null;$('inspection').hidden=true};$('transfer-tab').onclick=()=>tab('transfer');$('generation-tab').onclick=()=>tab('generation');$('findings').innerHTML=d.findings.map(f=>'<li>'+esc(f)+'</li>').join('');$('limits').innerHTML=d.limits.map(f=>'<li>'+esc(f)+'</li>').join('');$('run-note').textContent=d.counts.designs+' native constructions · '+d.counts.domains+' presentation domains · '+d.counts.packs+' connected packs · '+d.counts.applications+' applications · '+d.counts.transportChecks+' independent transport checks · '+d.counts.generationStages+' generation stages.';const params=new URLSearchParams(location.search);if(d.packs.some(p=>p.id===params.get('pack')))$('pack').value=params.get('pack');selectContext();if(pack().contexts.some(c=>c.id===params.get('context'))){$('context').value=params.get('context');renderTransfer()}if(params.has('case'))inspect(params.get('case'));if(d.generation.some(g=>g.id===params.get('scenario'))){$('scenario').value=params.get('scenario');selectScenario();if(scenario().stages.some(s=>s.id===params.get('stage'))){$('stage').value=params.get('stage');renderGeneration()}tab('generation')}else selectScenario();
})();
</script></body></html>
""";

    private static string Overview() => """
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Gojo · cross-domain construction atlas</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f7f5ee;color:#25434b;font:15px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1800px;margin:auto;padding:25px}h1,h2,h3{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:500}h1{font-size:38px;line-height:1.15}h2{font-size:28px;margin:30px 0 14px}h3{font-size:17px;margin:0;padding:10px 12px}a{color:#2c6971}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px}.card{background:#fffdf7;border:1px solid #cbd5ce;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0}.card img{display:block;width:100%;height:155px;object-fit:contain}.card p{padding:8px 12px;margin:0;font-size:12px;color:#65767a}.id{display:block;font:11px system-ui,sans-serif;color:#65767a}.intro{max-width:950px}.eyebrow{text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.13em;color:#65767a;font-size:12px}@media(max-width:1300px){.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:850px){.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:550px){main{padding:18px 12px}.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:8px}.card img{height:120px}h1{font-size:30px}}</style></head><body><main><div class="eyebrow">Gojo · native construction atlas</div><h1>Different domains, shared structural questions</h1><p class="intro">These 54 constructions deliberately mix matches, alternative mechanisms and counterexamples. Their domain labels organize the page; they are not part of the native matching evidence.</p><p><a href="gallery.html">Explore rule transfer and revisable generation</a></p><div id="cases"></div><h2>Symbolic templates and revised outputs</h2><div id="generation-cards" class="cards"></div></main><script src="data.js"></script><script>(()=>{const d=globalThis.RULE_PACK_TRANSFER,esc=v=>String(v??'').replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));document.getElementById('cases').innerHTML=['ORNAMENT','GLYPH','NETWORK'].map(domain=>'<section data-domain="'+domain+'"><h2>'+esc(domain[0]+domain.slice(1).toLowerCase())+'</h2><div class="cards">'+d.cases.filter(c=>c.domain===domain).map(c=>'<a class="card" data-case="'+esc(c.id)+'" href="gallery.html?pack='+encodeURIComponent(c.family)+'&amp;case='+encodeURIComponent(c.id)+'"><h3><span class="id">'+esc(c.id)+'</span>'+esc(c.name)+'</h3><img loading="lazy" src="'+esc(c.image)+'" alt="'+esc(c.name)+'"><p>'+esc(c.note)+'</p></a>').join('')+'</div></section>').join('');document.getElementById('generation-cards').innerHTML=d.generation.map(g=>{const outputs=g.stages.filter(s=>s.image);const chosen=[outputs[0],outputs.at(-1)].filter((s,i,a)=>s&&a.findIndex(other=>other?.id===s.id)===i);return chosen.map(s=>'<a class="card" data-scenario="'+esc(g.id)+'" href="gallery.html?scenario='+encodeURIComponent(g.id)+'&amp;stage='+encodeURIComponent(s.id)+'"><h3>'+esc(g.name)+'<span class="id">'+esc(s.name)+'</span></h3><img loading="lazy" src="'+esc(s.image)+'" alt="'+esc(s.name)+'"><p>'+esc(s.note)+'</p></a>').join('')}).join('')})()</script></body></html>
""";
